{%- comment -%}
  K&A Welcome Offer (KLP3000) — sitewide, engagement-triggered invitation
  card. Docs/welcome-offer-popup-build-spec.md (v2, revised).
  Prototype: Prototypes/welcome-offer-popup-v2.html — the current,
  authoritative prototype (welcome-offer-popup-v1.html is kept in the
  repo for reference/history only; do not build from it).

  v2 REVISION (2026-09-14), per Suraj's review of the staged v1 build:
  1. Email capture removed entirely — no {% form 'customer' %} block, no
     toggle, no success state, no tie-in to sections/ka-footer.liquid's
     Inner Circle newsletter signup. This file now has zero server-side
     form logic of any kind. The card is: eyebrow → amount → amount
     caption → code plate → CTA → fine print → dismiss. Nothing else.
  2. The amount (₹3,000) is now the card's primary visual element —
     largest, highest-contrast text on the card, replacing v1's separate
     italic headline (dropped: the oversized amount now does that job).
  3. Copy cut to the essentials (see assets/ka-welcome-offer.css for the
     v2.1 code-plate typography fix: the code value is set in --f-sans,
     not --f-display, to fix a real baseline-misalignment bug Suraj
     caught on the staged build).

  RENDERED FROM: layout/theme.liquid, once, sitewide, excluding the cart
  template (see the {%- unless request.page_type == 'cart' -%} guard at
  the call site) — NOT nested inside sections/ka-nav.liquid like the
  search overlay (snippets/ka-search-overlay.liquid), because there's no
  parent section to borrow `section.settings` from when rendering
  directly out of a layout file. Instead this follows the OTHER
  established pattern for a global, singleton, theme-editor-configurable
  overlay already in this codebase — snippets/ka-concierge-float.liquid —
  reading copy/config from global `settings.*` (config/settings_schema.json,
  "Welcome Offer (KLP3000)" group) rather than a per-instance section
  schema.

  ELIGIBILITY GATE (spec Section 2, condition 1) — server-side, before
  any client-side trigger logic gets a chance to run: a signed-in
  customer with at least one prior order NEVER receives this markup at
  all, not even hidden markup the JS could theoretically open. Also
  gated on the discount code setting being non-blank, so a merchant who
  clears the code field gets a clean "card doesn't exist" rather than a
  broken empty card (mirrors ka-voice-of-bride.liquid's own "don't ever
  publish placeholder/empty content" guard).

  Conditions 2-5 (no prior claim, no recent dismissal, once per session,
  not on cart / not while another overlay is open) are all client-side,
  in assets/ka-welcome-offer.js — see that file's header for the full
  state machine. "Claimed" now has exactly two paths in v2 (copy the
  code, or click the CTA) — v1's third path, email submission, no
  longer exists anywhere in this component.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Explicit step-by-step assigns rather than a single compound `and`/`or`
  condition — Liquid has no parentheses for grouping boolean logic, so
  `A and B or A and C` is genuinely ambiguous/error-prone to reason
  about correctly in one line. Same defensive style already used for
  ka-voice-of-bride.liquid's own has_synced_data / has_editor_content
  gate.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign is_returning_customer = false
  if customer and customer.orders_count > 0
    assign is_returning_customer = true
  endif

  assign should_render = false
  if settings.welcome_offer_code != blank and is_returning_customer == false
    assign should_render = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if should_render -%}
{{ 'ka-welcome-offer.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div class="ka-welcome-scrim" id="kaWelcomeScrim" role="presentation">
  <div class="ka-welcome" id="kaWelcome" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="kaWelcomeAmount">
    <div class="ka-welcome__handle" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <button type="button" class="ka-welcome__close" id="kaWelcomeClose" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>

    <span class="eyebrow ka-welcome__eyebrow">{{ settings.welcome_offer_eyebrow | default: 'A Welcome, From Us' }}</span>

    {%- comment -%}
      The amount — now the card's primary focal element (build spec v2
      Section 3). No inline `| default:` fallback with a literal ₹ symbol
      relied on here beyond the plain default below; the schema default
      (config/settings_schema.json) already guarantees this is never
      actually blank once the theme loads on Shopify.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="ka-welcome__amount" id="kaWelcomeAmount">{{ settings.welcome_offer_amount | default: '₹3,000' }}</p>
    <p class="ka-welcome__amount-sub">{{ settings.welcome_offer_amount_sub | default: 'toward your first piece, with our compliments' }}</p>

    <div class="ka-welcome__code">
      <span class="ka-welcome__code-label">{{ settings.welcome_offer_code_label | default: 'Code' }}</span>
      <span class="ka-welcome__code-value" id="kaWelcomeCodeValue">{{ settings.welcome_offer_code }}</span>
      <button type="button" class="ka-welcome__copy" id="kaWelcomeCopy" data-copy-label="{{ settings.welcome_offer_copy_label | default: 'Copy' }}" data-copied-label="{{ settings.welcome_offer_copied_label | default: 'Copied' }}">{{ settings.welcome_offer_copy_label | default: 'Copy' }}</button>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Native Shopify discount deep-link (build spec §5, Flag F1) — applies
      the code to the visitor's checkout session and redirects, zero app
      dependency. Real anchor href (not JS-only) so it works even if the
      claim-tracking JS below fails to attach for any reason; the click
      handler in ka-welcome-offer.js only adds the localStorage "claimed"
      write on top of this, it doesn't replace the navigation itself.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <a href="/discount/{{ settings.welcome_offer_code }}?redirect={{ settings.welcome_offer_redirect | default: '/collections/all' }}" class="ka-welcome__cta" id="kaWelcomeCta">{{ settings.welcome_offer_cta_label | default: 'Begin Shopping' }}</a>

    <p class="ka-welcome__fine">{{ settings.welcome_offer_fine_print | default: 'Valid toward your first order. Not combinable with other offers.' }}</p>
    <button type="button" class="ka-welcome__dismiss" id="kaWelcomeDismiss">{{ settings.welcome_offer_dismiss_label | default: 'Not today' }}</button>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endif -%}
